{"title":"2025 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the figure shown below, major arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55d147035986f87b2ae6889fd23fe148907adf75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{AD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> and minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cc93fbfb5ed16e87ce30594bc806a6094fe106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> have the same center, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Major arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55d147035986f87b2ae6889fd23fe148907adf75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{AD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" />, minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cc93fbfb5ed16e87ce30594bc806a6094fe106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" />, and each of the two segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />. What is the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd1ee80ffe3e3a92272f5af195c15051ea556aca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] usepackage(&quot;mathptmx&quot;); size(6cm); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); real r = 1 - pi + sqrt(pi^2 + 1); pair O = (0, 0), A = r * dir(-30), B = (r + 2pi) * dir(-30), C = (r + 2pi) * dir(30), D = r * dir(30); draw(arc(O, r, 30, 330)); draw(arc(O, r + 2pi, -30, 30)); draw(O--A, dashed); draw(O--D, dashed); draw(A--B); draw(C--D); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, dir(135)); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(270)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(0)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(0)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, 1.5 * dir(70)); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"265\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/8/918eb801cb5a5986d7adbda6da3c43086c118b2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}~1 - \\pi + \\sqrt{\\pi^{2} + 1} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}~\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}~\\frac{\\sqrt{\\pi^{2} + 1}}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}~2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"537\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Simple)\">Solution 1 (Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ratio between the radius and the arc length is constant. For the inner circle, the radius, which we will denote as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, has a corresponding arc length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b90c91b95f296eb61f1a5a9d6c1aa33307b637e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi r - 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" /> (the circumference minus the major arc length). For the outer circle, the radius, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa7a35d6a72333acabf36c967a59fa53b6424aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r + 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, has a corresponding arc length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />. We therefore write the equation \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bff7f55e0dca9220603032c08a35ef3e34cd20b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{r}{2\\pi r - 2\\pi} = \\frac{r+2\\pi}{2\\pi},\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"37\" />\nwhich simplifies to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b8abc31d3d8502168904939e7e89af6b1030620.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = (r+2\\pi)(r-1)\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea18e73dc5542e7a3020ad523847425b2ee49ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 = r^2 + (2\\pi-2)r - 2\\pi.\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" />\nApplying the Quadratic Formula, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/53526099146b064d20f6cfb44d70d1af3e88b453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r =\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} 1 - \\pi + \\sqrt{1 +\\pi^2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"204\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0fd5838af6da7c611be5e790ae71e357f985df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA=r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, which is the radius of the smaller circle. Then, the radius of the larger circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb65b76dd230432907697ec6491ca2be5735e0ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />. Indeed, we know that the length of major arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/9/a4936ee756bb350f48f3ff4603c9d315f8b7831a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{AD}=2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> and the length of minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/042ea6a88fa33d3c21b06291af6097bc0fdb189e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{BC}=2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />. So, using the formula for length of an arc formed by the central angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2d87c2746bf18130f641d2c6b17a0fa902f7863.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />, which we denote as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bfa6026e2848fb3951574bef7b50fa324c6cea4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\widehat{AD}=2\\pi=(2\\pi-\\theta) \\cdot r,\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"23\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a58860c9530564bcae5605dbd31717ff98ea776.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\widehat{BC}=2\\pi=\\theta \\cdot (2\\pi+r).\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>Expanding, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e0af9274c41bfbb4ac72422fc3ba63bb322d9e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\theta \\cdot r +2 \\pi \\theta = 2\\pi,\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/9842f8214a090e5b5988979365f302dbfca13ba8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\pi r-\\theta r=2\\pi,\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />\nand by adding the two equations we have that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cc1a67856f05e6860a95cf603d32bf339b372ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\pi \\theta + 2 \\pi r =4\\pi \\implies \\theta + r=2.\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Indeed, the question is asking for us to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and so we use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5a93c8f9fcd1a19ab92c031af544c6da87f353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = 2-r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> back into our original equation to solve:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d4135acf2667056ab13a6d301d501ad44850d9a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2 \\pi - \\theta) \\cdot r = (2 \\pi - 2 +r) \\cdot r = (2 \\pi -2)r +r^2= 2\\pi \\implies\\]\" width=\"448\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e8e6c67f29aa2fc461eb00678c2a929267c45e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2+(2 \\pi -2)r - 2 \\pi =0.\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Using the quadratic formula, we have that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/044fa4acfcd3304a010c260f0f5cefbb006259a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=\\frac{2-2\\pi \\pm \\sqrt{(2 \\pi -2)^2 - 4(1)(-2\\pi)}}{2}=\\frac{2-2\\pi \\pm \\sqrt{4 \\pi^2 -8 \\pi +4+8 \\pi}}{2}= \\frac{2-2\\pi \\pm 2 \\sqrt{1+ \\pi^2}}{2}= 1- \\pi \\pm \\sqrt{1+\\pi^2}.\\]\" width=\"881\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Since length must be positive, we consider only the positive root, and so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/5995d417f354259644f145fd64cf7ac87272cca0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} 1 - \\pi + \\sqrt{1 +\\pi^2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"171\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~e_is_2.71828\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BstSjBL0Bz8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BstSjBL0Bz8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dAeyV60Hu5c\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dAeyV60Hu5c</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Intuitive.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Intuitive)\">Video Solution (Intuitive)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Intuitive)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/O0Q53cYIe5I?si=xKqOMAt7DiNGNfko\">https://youtu.be/O0Q53cYIe5I?si=xKqOMAt7DiNGNfko</a> - Continuum Math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MadMath\">Video Solution by MadMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MadMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></spa